From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Take the XPC declarations the SDK already has

The iOS 26.2 SDK declares XPC in <xpc/xpc.h>, and <os/trace.h> includes it whenever the
SDK has it. USE(OS_LOG) is on for every Cocoa port and makes WTF/Assertions.h include
<os/log.h>, so the SDK's XPC declarations are in the translation unit of every WTF file. The
fallback typedefs and enumerators in XPCSPI.h then redeclare them with different types and
fail the build: Threading.cpp reported xpc_connection_t, xpc_endpoint_t and xpc_activity_t, and
the activity states.

The header now includes the SDK's <xpc/xpc.h> when the SDK has it, and keeps its fallback for
an SDK without it. HAVE_XPC_API is unchanged: the fallback still stands in for XPC on a build that
does not use the XPC API, so no XPC function is referenced by this change. A binary built for iOS 6
still must not import any xpc_* symbol; the import check on the stage proves it.
---
 Source/WTF/wtf/spi/darwin/XPCSPI.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/spi/darwin/XPCSPI.h b/Source/WTF/wtf/spi/darwin/XPCSPI.h
index 4bb236e..4070bcc 100644
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/spi/darwin/XPCSPI.h
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/spi/darwin/XPCSPI.h
@@ -33,7 +33,9 @@
 #include <os/object.h>
 #include <wtf/Platform.h>
 
-#if HAVE(XPC_API) || USE(APPLE_INTERNAL_SDK)
+// The SDK's own <xpc/xpc.h> is in the translation unit whenever a later SDK's <os/trace.h> is (USE(OS_LOG) pulls it
+// in through <os/log.h>), and then its declarations must stand in place of these.
+#if HAVE(XPC_API) || USE(APPLE_INTERNAL_SDK) || __has_include(<xpc/xpc.h>)
 #include <xpc/xpc.h>
 #else
 
